# Homepage Layout & RWD Sprint

**Based on:** HOMEPAGE_LAYOUT_RWD_AUDIT_REPORT.md  
**Sprint Goal:** Fix all 11 critical layout/RWD red flags with zero regressions  
**Target State:** Professional-grade responsive layout across all breakpoints and orientations

---

## Pre-Sprint: Regression Risk Analysis & Test Setup

### At-Risk Code Areas Identified

1. **Hero Component** (`app/components/features/homepage/hero/Hero.tsx`)
   - Risk: Padding changes affect text positioning
   - Risk: Button margin changes affect vertical rhythm
   - Dependencies: layout.tsx CSS variables

2. **Grid Component** (`app/components/layout/grid/Grid.tsx`)
   - Risk: Column changes affect all sections using Grid
   - Dependencies: IEMs Gallery

3. **IEMs Gallery** (`app/components/features/homepage/iems-gallery/`)
   - Risk: Header layout changes
   - Risk: Card sizing changes
   - Dependencies: Grid component, IemCard

4. **ProductSpotlight 1-3** (`app/components/features/homepage/product-spotlight-*/`)
   - Risk: Min-height removal affects section sizing
   - Risk: Grid breakpoint changes affect layout timing
   - Dependencies: Carousel system

5. **Carousel System** (`app/components/layout/carousel/`)
   - Risk: Breakpoint map changes affect all carousels
   - Dependencies: Featured, DACs, Accessories, NewestRelease

6. **Featured Section** (`app/components/features/homepage/featured/`)
   - Risk: Breakpoint map changes affect visible slides
   - Dependencies: CarouselContext

7. **DACs Section** (`app/components/features/homepage/dacs/`)
   - Risk: Breakpoint map changes
   - Dependencies: Carousel system

8. **Accessories Section** (`app/components/features/homepage/accessories/`)
   - Risk: Card height changes
   - Risk: Breakpoint map changes
   - Dependencies: CategorySection, AccessoryCard

### Regression Test Suite (Execute Before & After Sprint)

**Visual Regression Test Protocol:**
```bash
# 1. Build and start production server
npm run build
npm start

# 2. Run Playwright viewport tests
npx playwright test tests/homepage/viewport-regression.spec.ts --reporter=html

# 3. Screenshot comparison
# Compare against baseline in tests/homepage/baseline-screenshots/
```

**Unit Tests Required:**
- `tests/unit/Grid.breakpoints.test.tsx` - Verify column classes per breakpoint
- `tests/unit/CarouselContext.breakpoints.test.tsx` - Verify visibleCount calculation
- `tests/unit/Hero.layout.test.tsx` - Verify responsive classes applied

---

## Scope Contract 1: Design System Extension

**Objective:** Add xs breakpoint and landscape utilities to contain all fixes within design system

**DoD Sequence:**

### Layer 1 — Structure
- [ ] Add xs breakpoint to tailwind.config.ts screens
- [ ] Add landscape modifier utilities to safelist if needed

### Layer 2 — Layout
- [ ] Configure xs: 475px breakpoint
- [ ] Add xsPortrait/xsLandscape to CarouselContext breakpoint types
- [ ] Verify spacing scale applies to xs breakpoint

### Layer 3 — Surface
- [ ] No color changes
- [ ] No typography changes (already fluid via clamp())

### Layer 4 — Interaction
- [ ] No interaction changes

**Verification:**
- [ ] `npm run build` passes TypeScript compilation
- [ ] Test: xs breakpoint classes apply correctly (e.g., `xs:grid-cols-1`)
- [ ] Regression: Verify no changes to existing breakpoints (sm, md, lg, xl)

---

## Scope Contract 2: Grid Component Enhancement

**Objective:** Add xs breakpoint support for single-column layouts at narrow viewports

**DoD Sequence:**

### Layer 1 — Structure
- [ ] Modify `app/components/layout/grid/Grid.tsx`
- [ ] Add xs column variant to columnMap

### Layer 2 — Layout
- [ ] Update columnMap to support xs: `xs:grid-cols-1 grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4`
- [ ] Verify gap progression: `gap-4 md:gap-6 lg:gap-8` (no xs-specific gap needed)

### Layer 3 — Surface
- [ ] No changes

### Layer 4 — Interaction
- [ ] No changes

**Verification:**
- [ ] Test: Grid renders 1 column at < 475px when cols=4 specified
- [ ] Test: Grid renders 2 columns at 475-639px
- [ ] Regression: Verify existing sections using Grid still work (IEMs only)

